messages:
maria: Heads-up — PR #3456 updates the troubleshooting guide for timeouts, but I hit an intermittent 429 that the doc doesn't cover. Can folks weigh in on fallback order we should recommend? :thinking:

jules: repro steps? short requests or long?

maria: short-ish (prompt < 1k tokens). sometimes we get a 429 on retry 0 immediately after context trim landed in runtime. curl snippet:
```
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/generate -H 'Authorization: Bearer $KEY' -d '{"model":"rwd-3b","input":"hello"}'
```

olivia: hmm — thanks. I saw similar in staging last week when cache eviction coincided with very short bursts. I think the docs should recommend: 1) quick client-side backoff+retry, 2) local context trim (if available), 3) route to cheaper model variant, 4) graceful degrade. that order kept p99 latency low for us. :thumbsup:

sanjay: agree on backoff first. we should call out a specific backoff algorithm + jitter. propose: base 200ms, *2 exponent, max 2s, full jitter. Also note which errors are safe to retry vs which need idempotency checks.

kevin: I can add an SDK snippet for JS/py showing trim+retry combo. would be helpful to show how to trim prompts with tokenizer example.

engdocs: Please also add a crosslink to the Error Reference and to the Release Notes (context trim v2) so customers know why behavior changed. Also include a short bullet for Dedicated customers about routing policies — they can pin to the higher-capacity pool to avoid transient 429s.

maria: can we include a small decision table? e.g., when to trim vs when to switch model vs when to fall back to cached answer. makes triage faster for SEs.

jules: decision table + a tiny flowchart would be great. I'll sketch in the PR description.

kevin: quick draft JS retry+trim (will put in PR):
```js
async function generateWithTrim(client, prompt) {
  for (let i=0;i<4;i++) {
    try {
      const trimmed = maybeTrim(prompt, 2048);
      return await client.generate({model:'rwd-3b', input: trimmed});
    } catch (e) {
      if (e.code === 429) await sleep(Math.min(200 * 2**i, 2000) * Math.random());
      else throw e;
    }
  }
  // fallback to rwd-1b
  return client.generate({model:'rwd-1b', input: trimMore(prompt)});
}
```

olivia: nice. please add a short note above the code about safe trimming: never remove user-provided system instructions or last user message.

maria: action items: kevin add snippets (JS + py), jules add decision table + flowchart, engdocs add links + Dedicated note, sanjay add explicit backoff parameters text. I'll review once PR is up.

